              "paragraphs": [
                [
                  {
                    "t": "Andrea Carboni, the programmer of the game, said in an interview: “I never met Michael Tschoegl, who was contacted by Genias directly. The first music disk was completely broken when it arrived, so I recovered all that I could (almost) hear and composed the full tunes from the beginning. When I got the second disk, I realised that the tunes I modified, were not composed for the game parts I used them in. Moreover, they told me that my compositions were a lot better than his!!! Only the final track, the one that plays during the end titles (tune #6), remained untouched. Furthermore, I didn’t write about this on the title screen, since actually the basic sound was created by Michael anyway.” (info comes from an interview at "
                  },
                  {
                    "t": "www.retrogaming.it",
                    "url": "https://www.retrogaming.it"
                  },
                  {
                    "t": ")"
                  }
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
          "memoriam": false,
          "teaser": "Andrea Carboni, the programmer of the game, said in an interview: “I never met Michael Tschoegl, who was contacted by Genias directly.",
